@startuml
title M-SH3 - Independent session, execution, goal and board views (SH2+ target)
hide empty description

state "Session / delivery fence\nowner: swarma-session-host service process" as Session {
  state "Delivery open" as Open
  state "Fence closed\nbounded queue without delivery" as Closed
  state "Parked (durable)" as Parked
  state "Stopped by explicit stop / operator action" as Stopped
  state "Controller reconciliation" as Reconcile
  state "Controlled restart\nonly fence-holding operation" as Restart
  Open --> Parked : authorised park / unknown readiness / needs re-authentication
  Open --> Closed : close fence, including R-ALLSTOP; invalidate pending interactions
  Open --> Reconcile : controller failure; prohibit runner input
  Closed --> Reconcile : controller failure
  Reconcile --> Closed : evidence unknown / unreadable; retain permits
  Reconcile --> Open : verified re-adoption; reconciled fence, epoch and delivery evidence (§3.2-3.4)
  Open --> Restart : authorised restart; close fence / drain
  Parked --> Restart : explicit recovery (§3.5)
  Stopped --> Restart : explicit recovery; no automatic restart
  Restart --> Parked : unsupported row / unknown readiness or lock / surface drift (R-STANDING)
  Restart --> Closed : unknown process absence or delivery outcome
  Restart --> Open : process absence; admitted fresh runner confirms native-lock absence; readiness and reconciliation
  Open --> Stopped : explicit stop / operator action, including R-ALLSTOP; confirmed absence (§3.5)
  Closed --> Stopped : R-ALLSTOP; confirmed absence
  Parked --> Stopped : R-ALLSTOP; confirmed absence; no automatic restart
  Open --> Parked : journaled R-WATCH stop; record reason; keep fence if absence unknown
  note right of Parked
    No wake of parked or stopped sessions.
    Goal-free park has no board barrier.
    With board goal: optional board client acknowledges
    committed handoff revision by CAS.
    Bounded note attempt / marked snapshot fallback;
    timeout never proves drain (§3.5).
    Park wire/state schema: unspecified in spec §7.
  end note
  note left of Closed
    All effects carry fence / epoch / idempotent op_id rules.
    Operator update lock is distinct; only operator clears it.
    Prepare durable intent and closed fence before host_start.
    Fence change withdraws or reconciles affected start authority.
    Host failure retains dispatcher claim and closed fence.
    R-ALLSTOP: absence unknown keeps delivery closed and claims held; no Stopped transition.
    Exact per-effect state schema: unspecified in spec §3.4 / §7.
  end note
  note right of Restart
    Preserves standing session; replaces only its execution.
    host_stop -> confirmed prior-claim absence -> successor host_start.
    Session-scoped permit / owner session lifecycle authorisation (R-SESSION, §3.3).
    Replay logical_session_id / op_id returns the same successor.
    No lifecycle consent, retired owner, withdrawn/unknown permit: no successor.
    Dispatcher alone starts runner through claim / effect / root receipt.
    Fresh authenticated channel, current-epoch registration and readiness
    precede delivery. exec.stop proves process absence only.
    Fresh runner under agent account checks native-lock absence
    under closed fence and reports to host before harness initialisation / resume.
    Unknown native-lock result keeps session parked (§3.5).
    R-STANDING: executor verifies plan surface digests every launch / restart / native resume,
    or supplies from root-owned location outside home; drift refuses and reports.
    Repair only by explicit re-materialization; refusal code unpublished.
  end note
}

state "Execution (separate from session)\nrecords / capacity owner: swarma-dispatcher process" as Execution {
  state "Live authenticated runner\nswarma-session-runner / worker-<label>" as Live
  state "Stopping via swarma-user-manager exec.stop" as Stopping
  state "Confirmed execution absence" as Absent
  state "Unknown process evidence\ncapacity remains owned" as UnknownExecution
  Live --> Live : controller-only re-adoption keeps execution ID
  Live --> Stopping : host_stop / maintenance / journaled R-WATCH stop / R-ALLSTOP
  Live --> Absent : own exit; durable exit receipt and confirmed absence (§3.2, §3.5)
  Stopping --> Absent : latest receipt; TERM / KILL all UID processes; user domain stopped; quiet-period absence
  Stopping --> UnknownExecution : absence cannot be confirmed
  UnknownExecution --> Live : confirmed live authenticated runner (§3.2)
  UnknownExecution --> Absent : confirmed absence (§3.2)
  Absent --> Live : owner session lifecycle authorisation; successor host_start; new execution ID / current epoch / readiness
  note right of Absent
    Trusted standing executions have no preset runtime maximum.
    R-MAINT (§3.5 / dispatcher §11): close admission; inventory;
    stop selected executions with explicit operator authority via exec.stop.
    Deadline bounds maintenance attempt, never session / execution lifetime.
    Unknown/refused stop or incomplete reconciliation defers maintenance.
    Absence and reconciliation precede mode/state/binary changes;
    keep standing allocations / identities; R-MAINT withdraws permit; restart needs fresh owner admission.
    No live dispatcher adoption or automatic expiry.
    Dispatcher 12-hour maximum applies only to non-standing executions (§3.5).
    Only confirmed absence permits release / replacement.
    R-TRANSFER: home cleanup also needs recorded export or explicit operator waiver.
    Exit receipts are durable and replayable.
    Exit never satisfies optional board wait (§3.5).
    Runner owns Claude Code PTY / private Codex app-server transport and lease client.
    User manager owns root generation ledger and stop verification.
  end note
}

state "Wake / mail view\nbridge Mailbox and host inbox are distinct durable owners" as Wake {
  state "Mail held durably\nowner: agent-session-bridge" as Mail
  state "Host inbox pending\nowner: swarma-session-host" as Inbox
  state "Delivery held" as Held
  state "Host-directed turn-boundary input\nrunner writes harness transport" as Deliver
  state "Wedged: pending mail and neither idle\nnor progressing past deadline" as Wedged
  Mail --> Inbox : bridge enqueue; count delivery only after host durable write
  Inbox --> Held : closed fence / parked / stopped / needs re-authentication
  Inbox --> Deliver : open fence, ready boundary; current session/execution/epoch; admitted op_id
  Inbox --> Wedged : host detects deadline condition
  Wedged --> Inbox : host_stop / confirmed absence / authorised successor host_start; new epoch; immutable principal/id-to-complete-intent binding
  Wedged --> Held : park; host_stop; retain fence / claims if absence unknown
  note right of Held
    Producer / aggregate byte + count budgets apply even with closed fence.
    Bounded refusal / backpressure or journaled park / stop before reserve exhaustion.
    Retained debt survives replacement / retirement; incomplete evidence stays unknown (§7.20).
    No stale-session wake; no agent self-rearming / model wait.
    Runner reports boundary / idleness / heartbeat via readiness grammar.
    Unknown readiness parks (§3.7).
    R-TIME: monotonic wedge deadline; unknown reboot elapsed evidence is not guessed.
    Clock steps only narrow authority; deadline is not standing-session expiry.
    Deadline values / queue lifecycle details: unspecified in spec §3.7.
    Nudge / wake budget source, setter and default without board:
    unspecified in spec §3.8 / §7.
  end note
}

state "Optional goal command / acknowledgement\nrevision owner: host; board ledger owner: optional board" as Goal {
  state "No goal" as NoGoal
  state "Durable revision N" as Revision
  state "Deferred" as Deferred
  state "Applied acknowledgement" as AppliedGoal
  state "Rolled back with joined error" as RolledBack
  NoGoal --> Revision : authorised caller initial goal / board client revision (§3.8)
  Revision --> Deferred : host returns deferred
  Revision --> AppliedGoal : current runner turn boundary / harness acknowledgement
  Deferred --> AppliedGoal : optional compatibility adapter acknowledgement waiter (§2.3)
  Revision --> RolledBack : optional goal seam rollback
  note right of Revision
    Caller peer UID / active generation and scoped capability;
    actions, audience, expiry, revocation and open fence required.
    Wrong authority / stale epoch / revoked capability: refuse.
    Agent account has no goal capability (D-GOALS).
    Host-socket goal actions / capability shape and goal wire / ack:
    unpublished in spec §3.8 / §7.
    No specified agent "done" proposal path without board;
    any future proposal must not mutate a goal (D-GOALS).
    NoGoal does not gate any session operation (§3.8).
  end note
}

state "Optional board waiting / terminal view\nowner: board/orchestrator, initiating account" as Board {
  state "Board wait / completion barrier" as Wait
  state "Board terminal disposition" as Terminal
  note right of Wait
    Execution exit and goal acknowledgement do not imply board completion.
    Ledger / ancestry / outcomes / publication belong to board adapter.
    Agent outcome only proposes to board owner; it does not mutate a goal.
    Board state names, transition conditions and terminal enum:
    unspecified in spec §2.2 / §3.5 / §3.8; no transitions invented here.
  end note
}

note bottom of Session
  Views are conceptual, not newly specified wire enums or a combined FSM.
  Trusted standing sessions have no preset lifetime / runtime limit (§3.5).
  They end only by explicit stop, operator action or own exit.
  Park and controlled restart do not end them.
  Host loop: trusted class + local placement + admitted launch; circle membership insufficient.
  Remote placement remains workplace with donor loop even after circle admission.
  Emergency stop: operator authority, delivery closed, bound-board snapshot if any,
  host_stop under permit, fence / confirmed-absence receipts, explicit recovery (§3.5).
  host_stop is host-requested, distinct from owner cancel, and grants no start authority.
  Current / SH1 preserves tb-sessiond-owned transports and attached-client notices;
  target wake / park / cross-account goal gates are not activated by extraction.
end note
note bottom of Execution
  R-SESSION: host_stop only by configured host principal for execution under permit.
  Journaled E-stop / exec.stop / confirmed absence; host-requested, distinct from owner cancel.
  host_stop confers no start authority.
  R-FATE: user manager §7 owns process-class fate table beside R-FD3.
  Survival and service-swap affected set require published unit / per-OS evidence.
  Dispatcher supervisor writes fenced by daemon-instance epoch; no live adoption.
  F-13: latest receipt authorises stop; signalling / absence scope is all UID processes.
  R-WATCH v0: journaled dispatcher exec.stop; affected-session hold / status-only observer reads.
  No v0 per-account egress freeze or phone alert; v1 freeze lifecycle remains open.
  Host parks or ends with durable reason; unknown absence keeps fence / claims.
  R-ALLSTOP: manual operator act closes every session delivery and snapshots bound boards.
  Dispatcher hold; range deny-all; stop every generation; freeze leases / renewals.
  Delivered tokens keep vendor lifetime; direct same-act fan-out / per-service journals.
  Prompt independent cuts; receiver launch/create/activation fence before absence scan.
  Operator-helper stops progress without dispatcher; every durable part required before recovery.
  Unknown keeps admission closed; recovery names stopped set / restart scope / owner authority.
  Keep fences until confirmed absence; explicit recovery only, no automatic restart.
  R-SVC-EGRESS: host deny-all, including loopback TCP; Unix-socket calls only.
  Readiness needs verified service row / anchor / resolver restriction (user manager §8).
  F-15: authenticated controls / observation / already-authorised stop stay reachable
  while forward admission is closed; unknown records retain claims.
  R-LOCK: no state lock across dispatcher or runner call; durable in-flight marker.
  Late results revalidated under lock; stale results never reopen delivery / admission.
  Detailed host wait/lock graph: M-SH5 / spec §3.4.
end note
note bottom of Board
  R-TRANSFER: board accepts export as resource; orchestrator imports / reviews exact C / integrates.
  Positive review-role grant + trusted-class local agent or person; never producer / untrusted class.
  Circle alone grants no review; optional local-only / requester exclusion policies stay open / off.
  Exact-C inert diffs/blobs outside discovery roots; tree entry needs qualified strict adapter.
  No automatic candidate control adoption at startup / reload / nested read / resume / child entry.
  Acknowledge every flagged hunk with no prior load; acceptance is not control-context admission.
  Rework uses candidate base C and findings in new local task snapshot; never same-plan restart.
  R-VERIFY: tester orchestrates isolated ephemeral runners on another machine without secrets.
  Builds / tests / generators / worker-code execution never run in session account (R-EXEC).
  Results are data in board testing state; runner job/results formats unpublished.
end note
